caption: A tiddler whose header declares the dialect
type: text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki
title: Declares The Dialect
tags: [[Tag One]] TagTwo

A TIDDLER ANNOUNCES ITS DIALECT IN A FIELD, never in a filename. A wiki holds tiddlers rather than
files, so `type` carries the declaration that a `.mem` extension carries on disk — and the header
above lists its fields out of order on purpose, with `type` standing between a caption and a title,
because TiddlyWiki fixes no order and a rule reading this cannot assume one.

Everything from the blank line down reads as memetic-wikitext, so the dialect's own constructs
colour here exactly as they colour in a `.mem` file.

<<~ ahu #/the-body>>

! A heading inside the section

A sigil fires with a quoted value: <<~ stance "poet humorist">>, and a bearing carries its arrow in
<<~ lares aim from="lar://mara:operator@crossroads/operator.reads.the-declaration" -> to="lar://compita:agent@crossroads/clerk.answers.the-field">>

A local address stands at lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme and a digest at
ni:///sha-256;rwf5nn16-757tENuFe-t4Qz62-lTPMEAr4gOrxPb0Gs — two of them, so the pair of `//` runs
closes rather than opening an italic span that never ends.

